  issn = {0013-936X},
  doi = {10.1021/es015844c},
  abstract = {pdf in server. Paper copy opn file. Page 104 from another paper is appended. The subject matter was referred to in an email from Beate Escher send on May 2nd, 2002, as follows: Please find included a paper that appeared last week, where the work is included for which I tried out Absolv. My initial test set included 14 compounds, for which I had found descriptors for the solvation parameter model in the literature (references 48-50 in my paper). The result of the first set are depicted on page 104, which is appended to the paper. For the two missing compounds, 245Trichloroaniline and 2-Allylphenol. I estimated the alpha, beta etc values with Absolv. These values are included in the correlations in the Paper (at the end as supporting information)- reference to absolv ist given in ref. 51. As you can see, the two new values did decrease the quality of the fits, so I am wondering, if those are just difficult compounds or the estimations are not good. I also extracted the descriptors for the pharmaceuticals listed in Table 3. Since 3 of them are ionized at the pH of the experiments, it was not possible to set up a meningful LSER and I therefore did not use the estimated values and the corresponding LSER in my work. Thanks again very much for the trial use of Absolv. As you see, my work is not heavily relying upon the LSER models, but it was certainly an interesting excercise and I think it added to the understanding of the underlying molecular processes. Regards Beate},
